  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A current-carrying wire of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> and radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is suspended in a magnetic field of strength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"B\"></span>. The density of metal in the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rho\"></span> and the potential difference across the wire is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\"></span>. If the wire is stationary, what is the resistivity of the wire?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\varepsilon BL}{\\pi r^2\\rho g}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\varepsilon BL}{\\pi^2r^4\\rho g}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\varepsilon B}{\\rho gL}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\varepsilon B}{\\rho gL^2}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
